{
  "_id": "fhSubIronHour001",
  "name": "Ironhour Caps",
  "type": "consumable",
  "img": "icons/svg/item-bag.svg",
  "folder": "fhSubModern00001",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>Sealed glass vials of black-coated capsules sold under counter as \"jobsite supplements.\" The label is a knockoff of a defunct legitimate brand. Used by movers, longshoremen, and the desperate. Users swear every load feels half as heavy.</p><p><strong><em>Desired effects on use.</em></strong> For 1 hour you have advantage on Strength (Athletics) checks and a +2 bonus to Constitution saving throws.</p><p><strong><em>On use, save against addiction.</em></strong> Make a DC 13 Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, you gain the Addicted condition from Ironhour Caps (see below).</p><p><strong><em>Addicted from Ironhour Caps.</em></strong> While you have this Addicted condition, you are also Poisoned and have disadvantage on Dexterity saving throws (your reflexes feel a half-second slow).</p><p><strong><em>Withdrawal.</em></strong> At the end of each Long Rest while addicted, you either take another dose or abstain. If you abstain, make a DC 11 Wisdom check to resist the craving; on a failure, you give in and take a dose. On a success, you go into withdrawal for 3 days, or half that if you succeed on a DC 14 Constitution saving throw. If you have no doses left, skip the Wisdom check. While in withdrawal all your speeds are reduced by 10 feet, you have disadvantage on Strength and Constitution saving throws, and in combat you take 1d4 poison damage at the start of each of your turns. Abstaining then takes only the Wisdom check, and taking any dose ends the withdrawal but not the addiction. When the withdrawal ends, so does the addiction.</p><p><strong><em>Overdose.</em></strong> If you take a dose while still under its effects, or once your tolerance is at its limit, there is a 10% chance you overdose: you take 2d8 poison damage and have the Poisoned and Incapacitated conditions for 1 minute.</p><p><strong><em>Dosing others.</em></strong> As an action, you can slip a dose into food or drink within 5 feet. A creature that consumes it is dosed.</p><p><em>Requires ready paraphernalia that applies to ingested substances, such as a Pill Cutter, a Tincture Dropper or an Athlete's Logbook.</em></p>"
    },
